meta {
  name: 1 List inbox
  type: http
  seq: 1
}
get {
  url: {{gatewayUrl}}/api/v1/messages
  body: none
}
docs {
  Every message the caller is a **party to — sent as well as received**, scoped to the
  `NameIdentifier` claim. There is no address in the request, so nothing here can be pointed at
  somebody else's inbox.

  ⚠️ This used to filter on `recipient_email` alone, which made a conversation the caller
  **started** invisible to them: the mobile client groups this flat list into threads by `threadId`,
  so a thread with no received message had no rows to group and the Messages tab drew its
  "no messages yet" empty state over a live conversation until the other side replied.

  The body is a flat `MessageEntity` array — `id`, `senderEmail`, `recipientEmail`, `body`, `sentAt`,
  `isRead`, `threadId` — **one entry per message, not per thread**. Grouping into conversations is the
  client's job (`MessagingApiService.GroupIntoThreads`); there is no per-thread summary route.

  `threadId` is derived server-side as the two addresses sorted and joined with `::`, so it is stable
  whichever party sends first.
}
